Z||000006||lennyb4||06-14-2000||08:37 AM||||My brother is a cop and so are alot of my friends i grew up with. But i would have to say that there has been times (going 45 in a thirty zone) when i was busted cold, but they never do anything, they just watch me fly bye. Finally stopped one day and asked a cop why? He basicly said its because i've lived around there sooooo long, partied with almost all of them (and trust me when i say cops can PaRtY) and have friends on the force that they'll just tell my wife on me instead...NOOOOOOO!!!!!! (a fate worse then death)||||reg||6
Z||000007||Raydar||06-14-2000||09:27 AM||||The first time I drove my 88 coupe (bright red) through town, an officer pulled a "U-ie" in a parking lot, and followed me for several miles. Hasn't happened since. I guess they're used to me, by now. (The mall also opened, so I suppose they have other stuff to worry about.) ||||reg||1
Z||000008||2birds||06-14-2000||09:34 PM||||I'd swear my county (Camden, Georgia) has more Crown Vics per capita than any other, and they are all paid for with drug and DUI money.  I love it!!!<P>Our local cops seem to leave you alone if they recognize you and don't know you for a trouble maker.  They have better things to do, like stopping drug runners and DUI's, and keeping a lid on the violent crimes.  Everybody gets in a hurry now and then, just don't let it happen in a school or residential area, and you are generally OK.<P>My Fiero is cop-magnet red (only one like it in the area), so it's not like I blend in, but I won't say I never exceed the limit slightly.  <P>That movie is awesome.  Reminded me again of why I will never own a minivan...  I'd like to believe that 67 Mustang really had a 427 in it.  That sound made my skin crawl!  Big block Mustangs rule (as non-Fieros go, at least).  <p>[This message has been edited by 2birds (edited 06-14-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000009||stsmithgt||06-15-2000||07:34 PM||||It took me four whole days after getting my GT before I got pulled over and was called a speed demon.  I don't call 40 in a 30mph a speed demon, but I got off with a LONG warning so I shut up and smiled.  They did tag me for passing in a no passing zone which was B.S.  I didn't see the sign untill I went back to find it hidden in the bushes.  Besides I was passed that car before that sign.  I noticed they move the sign 50 feet closer so it's easier to see.  The cop almost ran over the car I passed to get to me!  I couldn't believed how reckless it looked in my rear view mirror.  I wasn't even speeding.  That's what I thought he was pulling me over for because I thought the speed limit was 30 and I was going 45, but the limit changed a block before to 45.  He was just being one of the rare asses in the force.  Oh well, you all have a good weekend.  I'm outa here!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lickout.gif">   ||||reg||1
